      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1000 divided doses at 850 mg. At this level the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max.\n- **1700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a more typical dose.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
